	(text "Upper I2C isolation. Discharge protection is out of scope. No charge FET, USB, or CAN.\nU_ISO is the ISO1640 8-pin D pin map from the ISO1640 datasheet Table 5-1. It has no enable pin.\nSide 1 (SDA1/SCL1) faces the host and is limited to 80 pF. Side 2 faces the upper BQ bus and allows 400 pF.\nVCC1 is HOST_3V3, 3 V to 5.5 V. VCC2 is upper REG1, 2.25 V to 5.5 V. Each supply gets 100 nF to its own ground (datasheet 9.2.1).\nGND1 is CELL0. GND2 is CELL16. Those grounds are not connected.\nSW_SDA and SW_SCL are the host-side disconnect. GPIO9 high = open. GPIO9 low = closed.\nGPIO9 low is what admits upper address 0x08, and only after the lower device is verified at 0x10.\nThe switch must stay off while unpowered and must not back-power HOST_3V3 from side 1.\nRise time must remain valid at 100 kHz with the side-1 pull-ups. Pull-up resistance is OPEN.\nUpper SDA/SCL pull-ups already sit on the upper sheet, on REG1_BQ2.\nOPEN parts:\nU_ISO: Bidirectional I2C isolator using the ISO1640 8-D pin map (VCC1, SDA1, SCL1, GND1, GND2, SCL2, SDA2, VCC2). No enable pin. Orderable suffix is OPEN; the 16-DW package has different pin numbers and is not this symbol.\nSW_SDA: Host-side SDA disconnect. MPN and footprint are OPEN. GPIO9 high = open, GPIO9 low = closed. Must isolate when unpowered and must not back-power the host rail.\nSW_SCL: Host-side SCL disconnect. Same requirements as SW_SDA.\nR201: Side-1 SDA pull-up to HOST_3V3. Resistance is OPEN at 100 kHz.\nR202: Side-1 SCL pull-up to HOST_3V3. Resistance is OPEN at 100 kHz.\nR203: GPIO9 reset pull-up to HOST_3V3. Value is OPEN. GPIO9 must be high at reset because GPIO9 low selects ESP32-C3 download mode."
		(at 20.32 229.87 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.05 1.05)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ac69d78c-7eaa-44df-bf78-9e0cf33c4d16")
	)
